      "content": "### 6.9.5.2 LBPM Definition and Transmission",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 528,
      "bottomRightX": 652,
      "bottomRightY": 559,
      "content": "LBPM is byte based with LSb transmitted first. A port may transmit a single LBPM, or consecutive LBPMs. The transmission of LBPM shall adhere to the following conventions.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 135,
      "topLeftY": 572,
      "bottomRightX": 657,
      "bottomRightY": 691,
      "content": "- A LBPM delimiter is defined with one tPWM of LFPS followed by one tPWM of EI.\n- The LPBM transmission shall start with a LBPM delimiter.\n- The LBPM transmission shall end with a LBPM delimiter.\n- The transmission of LBPM shall be LSb first.\n- Consecutive LBPM transmission shall be LSB first with LBPM delimiter in between each LBPMs.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "list"
